1
00:00:02,184 --> 00:00:05,582
Well, hello! Today, a trick
from the "wheel walk" family,

2
00:00:05,648 --> 00:00:06,700
the "koosh koosh".

3
00:00:06,716 --> 00:00:15,861
[Music]

4
00:00:15,861 --> 00:00:17,871
So, it's a fairly hard trick,

5
00:00:17,957 --> 00:00:21,808
it took me ages to tame,
but there are other variations

6
00:00:21,868 --> 00:00:23,241
that are a bit easier.

7
00:00:23,308 --> 00:00:24,386
As usual, start off

8
00:00:24,452 --> 00:00:27,180
holding on to a wall
to really feel what's going on.

9
00:00:29,074 --> 00:00:32,602
The first variation uses
one foot on the fork,

10
00:00:33,188 --> 00:00:37,420
which can block the tire,
while the other one scrapes.

11
00:00:38,868 --> 00:00:41,014
So you put your foot
here on the fork.

12
00:00:41,514 --> 00:00:43,360
You touch the fork and the tire.

13
00:00:43,399 --> 00:00:49,274
[Music]

14
00:00:49,274 --> 00:00:52,667
It's the easiest variation,
because every time you block the tire,

15
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:56,300
you can get back into position
over the wheel.

16
00:00:58,108 --> 00:01:01,646
In a second variation, you don't put
your feet right on the wheel,

17
00:01:01,732 --> 00:01:05,440
but to the side,
and drive it like this.

18
00:01:10,754 --> 00:01:14,540
So it's the arch of the foot here
that you place on the tire.

19
00:01:16,527 --> 00:01:19,380
You catch it very high up
and bring it down as far as you can.

20
00:01:22,421 --> 00:01:26,592
At first, it'll probably feel
like it's not gripping enough,

21
00:01:26,716 --> 00:01:28,782
and that you can't move
the wheel far enough,

22
00:01:28,906 --> 00:01:32,269
but don't worry,
you'll soon get the feel of it.

23
00:01:32,415 --> 00:01:36,914
Don't lean back, or hardly at all,
so your weight stays in the right place.

24
00:01:37,661 --> 00:01:40,951
At first, if the wheel
drifts every time

25
00:01:41,617 --> 00:01:43,960
and you zigzag, it's no big deal.

26
00:01:44,026 --> 00:01:49,488
[Music]

27
00:01:49,721 --> 00:01:52,639
Now let's see my favorite version,
with both feet behind the wheel,

28
00:01:52,783 --> 00:01:54,562
using the top of the foot.

29
00:01:54,829 --> 00:01:57,460
You'll probably spend a long time
holding on to the wall.

30
00:01:57,501 --> 00:01:58,528
That's fine, just do it.

31
00:01:58,593 --> 00:02:00,607
The position is pretty unusual,

32
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:04,620
and the foot movement
really takes some work.

33
00:02:05,228 --> 00:02:06,937
Foot position: two schools of thought.

34
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:12,061
Some people really lock the tire
between the toe here and the ankle.

35
00:02:12,561 --> 00:02:14,560
I find I'm more upright.

36
00:02:15,481 --> 00:02:19,413
I think putting your foot to the side
may give you more control over the wheel,

37
00:02:19,437 --> 00:02:20,920
especially when the tire is worn.

38
00:02:21,554 --> 00:02:24,640
Personally, I don't do it that way,
so I don't really have an opinion.

39
00:02:25,175 --> 00:02:26,848
Body position is very important.

40
00:02:26,921 --> 00:02:30,450
You tend to think you have to lean back
and end up leaning too far back.

41
00:02:30,594 --> 00:02:33,834
Actually, it's more about the hips
moving forward.

42
00:02:34,501 --> 00:02:36,230
Here, I'm sitting up straight
on my unicycle,

43
00:02:36,296 --> 00:02:38,943
and the position
means relaxing the hips...

44
00:02:39,443 --> 00:02:40,774
Here.

45
00:02:41,607 --> 00:02:45,088
Doing this puts my saddle
a little in front of me.

46
00:02:45,588 --> 00:02:48,591
That way, I can keep my body
over the hub

47
00:02:48,929 --> 00:02:51,380
and have more room
for my feet at the back.

48
00:02:51,928 --> 00:02:52,928
I hold on to the wall.

49
00:02:53,386 --> 00:02:54,693
I ease my hips forward.

50
00:02:54,759 --> 00:03:02,108
[Music]

51
00:03:02,108 --> 00:03:05,307
Getting into the trick is fairly easy
from a "wheel walk",

52
00:03:05,553 --> 00:03:08,615
from the pedals, from an "idle",
or from a "backward wheel walk".

53
00:03:08,887 --> 00:03:10,354
The "idle" seems easiest to me.

54
00:03:10,923 --> 00:03:14,840
From my "idle", just as the wheel
goes behind me, I place my foot.

55
00:03:14,906 --> 00:03:44,331
[Music]

56
00:03:44,331 --> 00:03:45,529
To get out of the trick,

57
00:03:45,553 --> 00:03:49,490
the easiest way is still to switch
back to a forward "wheel walk".

58
00:03:49,556 --> 00:03:54,958
[Music]

59
00:03:55,264 --> 00:03:59,051
It's harder, but it looks nicer:
you can catch the pedals straight away

60
00:03:59,124 --> 00:04:00,410
and carry on riding backward.

61
00:04:00,476 --> 00:04:13,841
[Music]

62
00:04:14,054 --> 00:04:15,819
Once you're comfortable with it,

63
00:04:15,885 --> 00:04:18,521
you can come up with variations,
like doing it with one foot,

64
00:04:18,587 --> 00:04:22,320
but without blocking the wheel
with the foot on the fork.

65
00:04:26,567 --> 00:04:28,420
Or even try it going forward.

66
00:04:33,274 --> 00:04:35,840
And of course, try to fit
all of this into your combos.

67
00:04:35,906 --> 00:04:54,870
[Music]
